[Music]  Google container registry is a private  container image registry that runs on  Google cloud platforms reliable fast and  secure infrastructure you can access  container registry through secure HTTP  endpoints which allow you to push pull  and manage images from any system VM  instance or your own hardware  additionally you can use the dr.  credential helper command-line tool to  configure docker to authenticate  directly with container registry while  docker provides a central registry for  storing public images you might not want  your images to be accessible to the  world to control access to your images  you must store them in a private  registry this hands-on lab demonstrates  how to build a docker image containing a  basic Python web app and push it to  Google container registry this lab is  also part of a series of labs called  quick starts these labs are designed to  give you a little taste of many features  available with Google Cloud search for  quick starts in the lab catalog to find  the next lab what you'd like to take  next up on our quest is deployment  manager QuickStart  [Music]

